From 229e94eb31a837f7ea11514e61207e2ee3d3876b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 16 May 2026 05:25:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] Plantard NTT: portable C plant path + cross-check +
 HAWK_PLANT_NTT flag
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Land the byte-identical-by-construction C 'plant' NTT path and the
infrastructure to wire it in:

  plant_18433.h / plant_18433.c
    External-linkage mq18433_NTT_plant / mq18433_iNTT_plant /
    mq18433_montymul_plant. Bodies are line-for-line copies of the
    Zq(NTT) / Zq(iNTT) / Zq(montymul) static inlines in modq.h with
    Q=18433, so they produce identical bytes by construction. The
    purpose of a separate translation unit is (a) to give the upcoming
    Cortex-M4 asm a stable, externally-linkable symbol set to replace,
    and (b) to provide a portable host fallback for the cross-check.

  hawk_sign.c
    Adds an opt-in macro layer: when HAWK_PLANT_NTT is defined to a
    non-zero value, the three hot mq18433_* entry points are macro-
    redirected to the _plant symbols. Default build (flag undefined)
    is unchanged.

  tests/test_plant_ntt.c
    The byte-equality cross-check called for in PLANTARD_NOTES.md:
    runs forward NTT, inverse NTT, and the fwd+inv roundtrip across
    logn in {8, 9, 10} (HAWK-256/512/1024) with multiple random
    polynomials, comparing mq18433_NTT vs mq18433_NTT_plant
    coefficient-by-coefficient. Currently ALL TESTS PASSED — that
    will continue to hold once the C body is swapped for the M4 asm
    (which is the whole point: the test is the safety net for the
    asm port).

Verified on host:
  * Default build: keygen -> sign -> verify roundtrip works.
  * HAWK_PLANT_NTT=1 build: same roundtrip works.
  * test_plant_ntt: byte-identical fwd/inv/roundtrip across all
    three parameter sets with many random polynomials each.
  * Existing tests (sha3 glue, plantard calibration) unaffected.

Next: drop in plant_18433_cm4.S with the hand-scheduled M4 kernel
(three-instruction reducer, packed-pair butterflies, layer-merged
2-3 layers per pass) and benchmark on NUCLEO-L4R5ZI. The asm has to
ship from an environment with an ARM toolchain so its assembly /
output can be verified against test_plant_ntt before enabling
HAWK_PLANT_NTT on the production path.
